"ref-3\" data-note=\"4e62b6beb4c1e82d\" href=\"?note=4e62b6beb4c1e82d\" title=\"58-df-ring-of-integers\">58-df-ring-of-integers</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|:V\\to V\">\\(|\\cdot|:V\\to V\\)</span> is the cardinality operator (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md\">../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IntegralConductor}_S:V^9\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{IntegralConductor}_S:V^9\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conductor\\text{-}integral\\text{-}order}\\vdash{}&amp;\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S(\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{RingOfIntegers}_S(\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\land\\mathcal O\\subseteq\\mathcal O_K\\land0_K,1_K\\in\\mathcal O\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathcal O\\;\\bigl(+_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle),\\cdot_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle)\\in\\mathcal O\\bigr)\\land\\forall a\\in\\mathcal O\\;\\exists b\\in\\mathcal O\\;(+_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle)=0_K)\\\\&amp;\\land\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\left(\\left|\\left\\{\\{+_K(\\langle a,x\\rangle):x\\in\\mathcal O\\}:a\\in\\mathcal O_K\\right\\}\\right|=n\\right).\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conductor\\text{-}integral\\text{-}order}\\vdash{}&amp;\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S(\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{RingOfIntegers}_S(\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\land\\mathcal O\\subseteq\\mathcal O_K\\land0_K,1_K\\in\\mathcal O\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathcal O\\;\\bigl(+_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle),\\cdot_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle)\\in\\mathcal O\\bigr)\\land\\forall a\\in\\mathcal O\\;\\exists b\\in\\mathcal O\\;(+_K(\\langle a,b\\rangle)=0_K)\\\\&amp;\\land\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\left(\\left|\\left\\{\\{+_K(\\langle a,x\\rangle):x\\in\\mathcal O\\}:a\\in\\mathcal O_K\\right\\}\\right|=n\\right).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conductor\\text{-}integral} \\vdash \\mathrm{IntegralConductor}_S(\\mathfrak f,\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S(\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\land\\mathfrak f=\\{a\\in\\mathcal O:\\forall x\\in\\mathcal O_K\\;(\\cdot_K(\\langle a,x\\rangle)\\in\\mathcal O)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conductor\\text{-}integral} \\vdash \\mathrm{IntegralConductor}_S(\\mathfrak f,\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{OrderInNumberField}_S(\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)\\land\\mathfrak f=\\{a\\in\\mathcal O:\\forall x\\in\\mathcal O_K\\;(\\cdot_K(\\langle a,x\\rangle)\\in\\mathcal O)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Conductor: measures ramification of representation or abelian extension</li>\n<li>Conductor-discriminant: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{f}^2 | d_K\">\\(\\mathfrak{f}^2 | d_K\\)</span> for abelian extension <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K/\\mathbb{Q}\">\\(K/\\mathbb{Q}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Artin and character conductors are distinct downstream notions and are not redefined in this order-conductor atom.</li>\n<li>Finiteness of the additive coset set is mediated by the registered cardinality operator; all cosets and products use the same displayed field operations.</li>\n<li>The source predicate <code>RingOfIntegers_S</code> has seven arguments.  Exposing that entire presentation removes the former two-place signature drift and the hidden multiplication in the conductor clause.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Neukirch, Algebraic Number Theory</li>\n<li>Cox, Primes of the Form <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x^2 + ny^2\">\\(x^2 + ny^2\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-ring-of-integers","status":"resolved","id":"4e62b6beb4c1e82d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ring-of-integers]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ring-of-integers","status":"resolved","id":"4e62b6beb4c1e82d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RingOfIntegers}_S:V^7\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ and $\\mathrm{RingOfIntegers}_S(\\mathcal O_K;K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota)$ (see [[58-df-ring-of-integers]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$|\\cdot|:V\\to V$ is the cardinality operator (see [[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"K,\\mathcal O,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak f,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,\\iota\\